# tests/suites.map — which tracked files each suite opens, so a pull request runs only the suites its change reaches
# (Tue Oct 27th 2026; tests/suitemap.sh holds the rules, CONTRIBUTING.md *CI* says how to keep this file).
# A push to main still runs every suite, so a miss here is caught there.
#
# Five kinds of line; a glob is a bash `case` pattern on the repo-relative path, `*` matching `/` too:
#   full <glob>…    a change to a matching file runs EVERY suite: the harness, the code every suite runs, and the gate's own tool.
#   none <glob>…    files no suite needs: a change to them alone runs no suite. Only files that are plainly not code, with the
#                   reason next to the line; code (lib/, bin/, contrib/ scripts, mod/ sources) never goes here. A suite that
#                   opens a file makes it measured, not none (--check fails a suite whose line names a none file, except a firstline suite).
#   text <suite>…   suites that read files as text across the repo (syntax parses every file; lanefields greps lib/ and web/).
#                   They still run on a change that is only comments and blank lines in a shell or Python file.
#   firstline <suite>…   suites that open every tracked file only to read its first line (syntax's shebang test). --measure leaves
#                   none files off THEIR lines and no others': lanefields reads README.md as content, so README.md is not none.
#   suite <name> <file>…   MEASURED, one line per suite, files sorted: the tracked files the suite opened when it ran under
#                   strace, minus the `full` files and the suite's own tests/<name>.sh. Written by
#                   `bash tests/suitemap.sh --measure <name>…`; NEVER edited by hand (the next measure rewrites the line).
# `bash tests/suitemap.sh --check` fails a PR when a suite has no line, a tracked file is neither full, none nor on a line, or a
# line names a file that is gone.
#
# full: the shared code and harness every suite runs through (bin/salamander, lib/common.sh and lib/boardlinks.sh, which it sources, lib/api-credit.sh, which common.sh sources, tests/lib.sh, tests/run.sh,
# tests/fake-claude.c) and the tool that reads this file (tests/suitemap.sh).
full bin/salamander lib/common.sh lib/api-credit.sh lib/boardlinks.sh tests/lib.sh tests/run.sh tests/fake-claude.c tests/suitemap.sh
# none: prose and repository housekeeping that no suite parses, named file by file. NOT `*.md`: the briefing's model prompts
# (contrib/briefing/*.prompt.md) are text the briefing suite feeds a fake claude, so they are measured. The launchd plists are
# XML for macOS boxes that only launchd reads (syntax.sh opens their first line to look for a shebang, which a firstline
# suite's line does not count). README.md is NOT here: tests/lanefields.sh greps it for the lane-fields section.
none docs/* CONTRIBUTING.md contrib/briefing/README.md LICENSE .gitignore */.gitignore launchd/*
# text: the suites that read most of the repo as data.
text syntax lanefields
# firstline: opens every tracked file for line 1 only.
firstline syntax
